Licensing notice for the data/ directory
=========================================

The files in this directory are NOT all covered by the MIT license at the
repository root. Three different licenses apply, depending on where a given
field originated:

1. data/dog_rules.json and data/extra_beaches.json: CC BY-NC 4.0
   -----------------------------------------------------------------
   These two files are BeachPaws' hand-curated dataset: dog-access rules
   sourced from council Public Spaces Protection Order (PSPO) pages, and a
   handful of beaches not in the Environment Agency's designated-bathing-water
   list. Curating and keeping this accurate is manual, ongoing work and is
   this project's commercial differentiator.

   These two files are licensed under
   Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0):
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

   In short: you may share and adapt this data with attribution, for
   non-commercial purposes. Commercial use (including bulk redistribution,
   resale, or feeding it into a commercial product or service) requires a
   separate license from the copyright holder. This notice is a summary, not
   a substitute for the full license text at the link above.

2. data/beaches.json: mixed, generated
   -----------------------------------------------------------------
   This file is pipeline output (see scripts/build_data.py) and combines
   fields from both of the following sources on a per-beach basis:

   - Location, sediment type, and water-quality fields are sourced from the
     Environment Agency's Bathing Water Quality API and remain licensed under
     the Open Government Licence v3.0 (OGL v3):
     https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
     These fields are NOT subject to the CC BY-NC non-commercial restriction;
     OGL v3 already permits commercial use, and nothing here narrows that.

   - The `dogs` field on each beach entry is joined in from data/dog_rules.json
     (or absent, for beaches with no curated entry) and is covered by the
     CC BY-NC 4.0 terms described above.

   Because beaches.json interleaves both, treat each field according to its
   source rather than the file as a whole: EA-derived fields stay OGL v3,
   `dogs` stays CC BY-NC 4.0.

3. data/config.json and data/counties.json: MIT
   -----------------------------------------------------------------
   These are small structural/config files (an API country selector, and a
   district-to-county lookup) with no independent creative or curated content.
   They fall under the repository's root MIT license, same as the code.

Every entry in data/dog_rules.json carries its own `source` (the council page
it was checked against) and `accessed` (the date it was checked). Please
preserve both when reusing this data, per the CC BY-NC attribution requirement.
